<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the second</p>
<p>day of four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Thursday:</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham v Hampshire - no play due to</p>
<p>rain.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 280 (D.Robinson 78, P.Prichard 51;</p>
<p>J.Kerr 4-83). Somerset 249-6 (P.Holloway 90, M.Lathwell 87).</p>
<p>At Swansea: Glamorgan 319-3 (H.Morris 158 not out), M.Maynard</p>
<p>98) v Gloucestershire.</p>
<p>At Maidstone: Kent 306 (N.Llong 57, P.Strang 55; M Akram</p>
<p>4-56) v Northamptonshire 41-0.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Yorkshire 268 (D. Byas 88; A.Mullally 5-103) v</p>
<p>Leicestershire 5-1.</p>
<p>At Uxbridge: Middlesex 118 (P.Martin 8-32). Lancashire 309-4</p>
<p>(N.Fairbrother 82 not out, S.Titchard 79, N. Wood 67).</p>
<p>At Arundel: Worcestershire 255 (S.Rhodes 58 not out) v Sussex</p>
<p>23-3.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Surrey 193 (G.Welch 4-62, A.Donald 4-64) v</p>
<p>Warwickshire 159-4 (D.Brown 57 not out).</p>
</text>
